WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the russian invasion was launched with  terrifying speed and against a wide  range of targets right across the  country  the long military buildup around  ukraine's borders finally unleashed by  order of the kremlin  helicopter gunships fighter jets  missiles tanks convoys of armored  vehicles are all involved in what russia  calls a military operation  for the moment the targets appear to be  specific and strategic they include  ukraine's airfields and military bases  this video from molitopol in southern  ukraine appears to show the destruction  of the city's airfield  the shrapnel and shells are also  reported to have landed in civilian  areas  including the capital kiev  until the very last moment i didn't  believe it would happen i thought it  might just involve donetsk and luhansk  but i didn't ever think it would involve  kiev  most likely war has now begun everyone  is leaving everywhere is shut  i hate the country that started this war  i speak as a mother and as a ukrainian  and i call on the whole world to help us  and stop this aggressor  ukraine's government declared martial  law  [Music]  i had a conversation with us president  joe biden the u.s is starting to gather  international support  today we need you each of you to be calm  if possible stay at home please we are  working the army is working the entire  security and defense sector of ukraine  is working  the russian military offensive follows a  carefully choreographed strategy of  russia's president vladimir putin  he unilaterally recognized two  separatist regions in eastern ukraine as  independent of kiev and then sent  russian soldiers in under the pretext of  being peacekeepers  the battle for luhansk and donetsk in  eastern ukraine has been going on since  2014  with more than 14 000 people killed in  fighting between the russian-backed  separatists and the ukrainian army  now what putin calls peacekeepers are on  the attack and the russian leader is  warning ukrainian soldiers not to resist  when you put themselves whoever would  try to stop us and further create  threats to our country to our people  should know that russia's response will  be immediate and lead you to such  consequences that you have never faced  in your history we are ready for any  outcome  the russian invasion began despite  last-ditch appeals from members of the  united nations security council to ease  tension  ukraine's ambassador to the un demanded  his russian counterpart stepped down as  chairman call putin called lavrov  to stop aggression  there is no purgatory for war criminals  they go straight to hell ambassador  as news of the invasion spread in  ukraine's capital kiev main highways out  of the city quickly became gridlocked  with traffic  there's a mood of desperation developing  now many people just jumping into their  cars getting their families together and  heading on the road trying to get to  poland  but the main auto routes are all jammed  there are so many people trying to do  the same thing others are going  underground taking shelter  others have been flocking to the  supermarkets and frantically stocking up  on essential items  this was the scene in kramatorsk in the  east of ukraine as shoppers grab what  they could to fill their cupboards  the ukrainian army and air force are  putting up a fight and resisting the  russian attack  this video from the defense ministry  said to show a russian helicopter shot  down by ukrainian forces near kiev  but there will be no reinforcements from  nato  and the odds look heavily stacked  against ukraine's forces  andrew simmons al jazeera kiev

